{
  "about": "Odds tables for the consequence engine (companion/consequences.py). Each choice lists its options in the order the code knows them. An option starts at its weight; every rule whose reader matches multiplies the weight by `times` and adds its `why` to the reasons shown in \"Why it went this way\". Readers: drama (0 quiet to 3 soap opera), closeness_a / closeness_b (how close the companion is to the first / second person in the story, 1 to 5), tie (how the two people know each other: old friends, friends, coworkers, family, married), age_a (the first person's age), sheet (words in the companion's own description; the word groups are in the code), minds (for the user:* choices: 0 to 3, the intensity of an emotional trait the user built into the character that speaks to it; names {trait}), mood and money (the sum of the marks earlier outcomes left on the companion, negative for low or tight). An option's `marks` are what it leaves when picked: kind mood or money with an amount, or avoid (keep away from `about`), on me, a or b, for `days`; `ripple` also reaches the companions who feel close to them; `told` is how the companion carries it, told to them as \"you\" in the chat context. The user:* and chapter:* choices name each option's `label`; can_<kind> (1 or 0) says whether that life chapter is possible at all, and friends counts the friends in their circle. Names in `why`: {name} the companion, {a} and {b} the people in the story.",
  "choices": {
